{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for exact17be8b9b1f819610fd4331bd0be65065ae4ae4f3/treec77c294ccceac04d346dc06b7c92e12225647ceb. Read primary5ad117e0 first, full reconciliation note and full15.3 amendment, complete two-note delta, native creates()/namedBy grammar and adopted191d8dec/78127fe6. The purposes, typed edges, validation-before-recursion, cumulative allowance, failed probes versus selected dependencies, omission/no-tombstone rule and unchanged ordinary replay are aligned. Two narrow contract corrections are needed before this becomes the inventory Source's table.\n\nF1/P2: section15.3's Kind column still omits definition for outcome and delivery. The outcome evidence and observation consumers, and delivery observation consumer, can name DOMAINS.definition; approved retained-key prerequisite8550dadd/573c3b42 now reads those exact dependencies as kind definition, with no value-domain component. The general child-closure row covers their children, not the root key missing from these per-variant rows. Add definition to both rows and state that typed definition-domain roots themselves are replay-required under the native retained key, while their extra static children are archive-closure. This keeps the table's per-variant coverage requirement consistent with actual supported consumers; no alias or ordinary replay expansion.\n\nF2/P2: section15.3 says any input a later turn retains is outside the cutoff. With the new stronger closure this is false: a root selected at cutoff can already statically name an unused child whose bytes are initially absent (the preceding paragraph explicitly permits that native founding case). If those child's immutable bytes become available later, they remain required by the same fixed cutoff and can let its previously incomplete manifest complete. Rewrite the exclusion in terms of names/dependencies: inputs named only by entries after the cutoff are excluded; later availability of an already named root/closure dependency d